<Base title="Data handling for clinics" description="Where clinic data lives, who processes it, how long it is kept and how it leaves. The public version of our data processing agreement.">
  <article class="wrap narrow hero prose">
    <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/vets">For veterinary teams</a> · Data handling</p>
    <h1>Where your data goes, and where it doesn't</h1>
    <p class="lead">This page is the public version of the data processing agreement every clinic signs with us. If something here is not in the contract, the contract is wrong. Status: draft until the first pilot clinic signs; what changes will be listed at the bottom.</p>

    <h2>Roles</h2>
    <p>Your clinic is the controller of its clinical records. AI Veterinary is a processor acting on your documented instructions (Art. 28 GDPR). We never use clinic data for our own purposes, and nothing is used to train AI models, ours or anyone else's.</p>

    <h2>What is processed</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your typed notes, the structured record built from them, and the documents you approve. These are one unit: a document is never stored without the notes it came from.</li>
      <li>Patient identity: name, species, breed, sex, date of birth, microchip. Owner identity only as far as a document needs it (name, and the tax identifier where a country requires it on an invoice or prescription).</li>
      <li>Account data of your team members (name, email, role) and an append-only audit log of who approved what, when.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No audio. The assistant has no microphone feature, so there is nothing recorded and nothing to ask owners to consent to.</p>

    <h2>Subprocessors</h2>
    <p>The complete list. You are notified 30 days before any addition and may object.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Location</th><th>Clinical content?</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Cloudflare</td><td>Hosting of the website and application, TLS, DDoS protection</td><td>EU edge, global network for static assets</td><td>Passes through encrypted; not stored</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Supabase</td><td>Database, authentication, file storage</td><td>Frankfurt, Germany</td><td>Yes, encrypted at rest; access restricted per clinic by row-level security</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Anthropic</td><td>Language model that structures notes into the record</td><td>EU region where offered; otherwise under standard contractual clauses</td><td>Yes, for the duration of the request; no training; shortest retention the provider offers (zero-retention where available)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Email provider (to be selected, EU)</td><td>Transactional email: login links, approval notifications</td><td>EU</td><td>No</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>There are no analytics scripts, advertising pixels or session recordings on the application.</p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Kept for</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Clinical records, notes, approved documents, AI generations</td><td>As long as your clinic decides; many countries require multi-year retention of veterinary records and your clinic sets that period</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Audit log</td><td>At least as long as the record it belongs to</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Application logs (redacted, no clinical content)</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Backups (encrypted, in region)</td><td>35 days, then overwritten</td></tr>
        <tr><td>After account closure</td><td>Full export offered first; deletion within 30 days; backups age out within 35 days; confirmed in writing</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Your rights as a clinic</h2>
    <ul class="paw-list">
      <li><strong>Export anything, any time.</strong> Every record and document, with its notes and audit trail, as JSON and PDF. No fee, no notice period.</li>
      <li><strong>Owner requests go through you.</strong> When an owner asks for access or erasure, you decide; we give you the tools to fulfil it.</li>
      <li><strong>Audit us.</strong> On request we provide our security documentation, subprocessor contracts and, once in place, third-party audit reports.</li>
      <li><strong>Breach notice within 24 hours</strong> of us becoming aware, with what we know and what we are doing.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Templates for your own obligations</h2>
    <p>Available with the pilot agreement: an <em>Auftragsverarbeitungsvertrag</em> (Art. 28) for German and Austrian practices, a Swiss DSG addendum, and an <em>Informativa sull'uso dell'intelligenza artificiale</em> for Italian clinics that want to inform owners about AI-assisted documentation.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
    <p>None yet. Every change will be dated here. Questions: <a href="mailto:privacy@aiveterinary.org">privacy@aiveterinary.org</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
